window.EN={"1":"With the fall of King Zephiel, the kingdom of Bern surrendered.","2":"The great upheaval that had engulfed the continent had, for the moment, come to an end here.","3":"But the fight for Roy and the others was not yet over.","4":"Pursuing the \"Priestess of Darkness,\" who was highly likely to be the \"Dragon-Devil,\"","5":"and relying on the streak of light that the \"Divine Weapons\" pointed to,","6":"they advanced their army toward the \"Shrine of Dragons,\" once the home base of the \"dragons\" of old.","7":"But before the \"Shrine of Dragons,\" General Brunnya, the last of Bern's Three Dragon Generals, leading Bern's remaining forces,","8":"wagers the pride and honor of being \"the continent's strongest\" and challenges Roy and the Etrurian army to one final battle.","9":"Against a kingdom of Bern that no longer exists in this world,","10":"the fight against these \"ghosts\"","11":"casts a dark shadow over the hearts of Roy and the others...","12":"Well then, Lord Yarne, I entrust Lady Idunn to your care, without fail.","13":"What will you all do? You humans.","14":"We will challenge the Etrurian army to one more battle, here.","15":"Do you have the fighting strength for it?","16":"The Bern wyvern knights, who had been scattered across the land, have gathered to our side.","17":"Do you have any chance of victory?","18":"...It's by no means high. But we are the army of Bern, the strongest kingdom on the continent.","19":"We should be able to show you that \"pride\" of ours.","20":"\"Pride,\" is it... you humans sometimes act for reasons that go beyond our understanding.","21":"Can this thing called \"pride\" really raise the chances of victory?","22":"Well, fine. We will fight in our own way.","23":"...Did you convey my words to everyone?","24":"Yes, sir.","25":"\"Even those who leave the army from here on will not be charged with the crime of desertion.","26":"Whether to stay and fight, or to leave this place, is left to each person's own judgment,\" I told them.","27":"And so, how many remained?","28":"Nearly everyone has said they wish to fight alongside you, Lady Brunnya.","29":"Everyone?","30":"This isn't a battle with good odds of victory. There must be those among them with families waiting for them.","31":"There's no need to force yourselves to keep me company in my fight.","32":"We too are knights of Bern.","33":"We have no intention of obeying those who shamefully submitted to Etruria's rule.","34":"...Those with the wounded, those with young children, and those with aged parents—remove them by force.","35":"But, Lady Brunnya...","36":"This is an order. Understood?","37":"...Lord Roy, our allied army's deployment is complete.","38":"Did you send an envoy to the enemy?","39":"Yes.","40":"As expected... it seems they have no intention of surrendering to our army.","41":"What about the fact that if they surrender, their lives will be guaranteed?","42":"Of course, I conveyed that as well... but","43":"they said: \"We're grateful for the offer, but we have no intention of surrendering.\"","44":"Why is that? The kingdom of Bern has already surrendered, and yet...","45":"...I imagine this person here would know the answer to that.","46":".........","47":"Princess Guinevere... do you understand it, Princess?","48":"Yes.","49":"...The kingdom of Bern's army prides itself on being the strongest on the continent.","50":"Surely that pride and sense of honor won't allow them to accept defeat to another nation.","51":"That's so...","52":"Lord Roy! The enemy has begun to move!","53":"There's no helping it. Let's fight! Marinas, take Princess Guinevere to the rear...","54":"No, please, let me stay here too.","55":"I must take in their cries myself.","56":"That's the very least I can do, I who ended up betraying Bern as a result...","57":"Princess Guinevere...","58":"C-Lord Karel, soon... this place too will become a battlefield...","59":"I see.","60":"This village is a place unknown to those who live in other lands.","61":"I had thought that as long as we stayed here, we wouldn't get caught up in war, but...","62":"What should we do...","63":"Don't worry. If it comes to that, I'll protect the village.","64":"Oh, that's a great relief.","65":"If we can be protected by Lord Karel, known as the \"Sword Saint,\"","66":"there's nothing at all for us to fear.","67":"I'm just an ordinary swordsman, you know.","68":"People's rumors are the sort of thing that swell the more time passes.","69":"...Still, it seems this war has grown larger than I'd thought.","70":"I wonder if my little sisters are all right...","71":"...I had no idea you had siblings, Lord Karel. This is the first I've heard of it.","72":"It's been a long time since I last saw their faces, but I heard through others that one fell ill.","73":"I can only hope she's recovered and is living a settled life now, with her husband and daughter, the three of them together.","74":"※If visited with Fir","75":"Uncle!","76":"That voice... is that Fir...! What are you doing in a place like this?","77":"Uncle, the same goes for you—why are you in this land?","78":"After traveling from place to place, I settled down here.","79":"I thought that here, at least, I could pursue the way of the sword without getting caught up in the world's conflicts, but...","80":"Uncle, there's something I must tell you...","81":"It's... Mother...","82":"...Has she died?","83":"Yes...","84":"...","85":"I see. So she couldn't be saved, then...","86":"I'm sorry. I couldn't be by her side in such a difficult time.","87":"No, it's...","88":"But why are you here, of all places?","89":"Judging by your appearance, it doesn't seem you were searching for me just to tell me that?","90":"Yes. Right now, I'm fighting against Bern's army.","91":"Joining in a war...? Is that what you mean?","92":"I know that you, Uncle, dislike conflicts between people.","93":"But I couldn't bring myself to overlook the people suffering under this drawn-out war...","94":"Uncle, am I wrong to feel this way?","95":"Is it not right, for one who aspires to the way of the sword...?","96":"No, that's not true at all. The path you walk is not a mistaken one.","97":"I will lend my strength to that same path as well.","98":"Really?!","99":"Yes... ...you're right, after all.","100":"Heh... you've grown. And here I thought you were still a mere infant.","101":"Uncle...","102":"※If visited with Bartre","103":"C-Lord Karel!","104":"...Could that be Lord Bartre? Why are you in such a place as this?","105":"I'm currently with the Etrurian army, fighting.","106":"What of you, Lord Karel—why are you here, of all places...","107":"After traveling from place to place, I settled down in this land.","108":"I thought that here, at least, I could pursue the way of the sword without getting caught up in the world's conflicts, but...","109":"...Actually, there's something I must apologize to you for, Lord Karel...","110":"...Is it about my sister?","111":"Indeed... I did everything I could, but...","112":"She couldn't be saved, then...","113":"I'm sorry! Even with me there by her side...","114":"It's hardly your fault, Lord Bartre.","115":"If anyone must apologize, it's me.","116":"I couldn't do anything for her, in such a difficult time.","117":"...Lord Karel, I have a favor to ask.","118":"What might it be?","119":"I want this war to end soon.","120":"I know that you, Lord Karel, dislike war, but","121":"won't you fight alongside us?","122":"...Very well, Lord Bartre. I too will do what I can.","123":"I'm grateful!","124":"If you lend us your strength, Lord Karel, nothing could be more reassuring!","125":"※If visited with any other unit","126":"There's no one in this village connected with the war.","127":"I'm sorry, but would you mind leaving?","128":"You're Lord Roy, then?","129":"And you are?","130":"I am Karel. I've come to be allowed to join this army.","131":"Pleased to make your acquaintance.","132":"You're the \"Sword Saint\"...","133":"I've heard about you. Said to be the owner of an incredible sword arm.","134":"The pleasure's mine as well. Thank you for having me.","135":"※If fought with Melady: You... Melady...","136":"I see. So you intend to walk the same path as Her Highness Guinevere.","137":"That too may well be one path to take...","138":"But I, too, cannot yield on Bern's pride!","139":"※If fought with Zeiss: You are... one of Bern's wyvern knights...","140":"I see. So you intend to walk the same path as Her Highness Guinevere.","141":"That too may well be one path to take...","142":"But I, too, cannot yield on Bern's pride!","143":"※If fought with any other unit: Bern will not fall!","144":"Even should we fall here, we will be reborn, again and again!!","145":"My lord... with this... at last... I'll be by your side...","146":"So this is the \"Shrine of Dragons\"... does that mean the \"Priestess of Darkness\" is somewhere inside?","147":"Judging by the circumstances, there's little doubt. There is, however, something that concerns me...","148":"What is it?","149":"In one account of the legend concerning the Scouring...","150":"...it's said the \"Shrine of Dragons\" holds within it the power of the \"dragons\"...","151":"something along those lines exists.","152":"I wonder what that means.","153":"It could also mean the power of the \"dragons\" protects the \"dragons\" themselves.","154":"The power of the \"dragons\"... protecting the \"dragons\"...","155":"...That only confuses me more.","156":"...This is just my own interpretation, but","157":"might not the \"dragons\" within the \"Shrine of Dragons\"","158":"hold some kind of power stronger than those outside it?","159":"In other words, our usual way of fighting might not work... is that what you're saying?","160":"Yes.","161":"But still... if we combine someone with power equal to the \"Eight Generals\" with a \"Divine Weapon\" as well,","162":"perhaps...","163":"So you're saying we should follow the example of the \"Scouring\" once more.","164":"...There isn't really any other good method available, is there...","165":"All right! Then let's go in with only those who have particularly strong power!","166":"The choice of who you bring with you should be made carefully...","167":"Once we go in, there's a chance we won't easily be able to come back..."};
